@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Explicit chat and bounded provider response handling
hide footbox
autonumber
actor User
participant "Assistant\n<<React function>>" as Web
participant "main.chat\n<<route function>>" as API
participant "grounding / dataset / dictionary\n<<modules>>" as Local
participant "service : GeminiService" as AI
participant "httpx / Gemini" as Provider

activate User
User -> Web : Send message
activate Web
Web -> Web : makeHistory(successful messages)
activate Web
Web --> Web : Up to 6 complete exchanges; <= 24,000 chars
deactivate Web
Web -> API : POST /api/chat\nChatRequest
activate API
opt use_dataset or use_dictionary
  API -> Local : retrieve(..., chat=True)\nusing current + last 2 user queries
  activate Local
  Local --> API : Source-labelled evidence / storage error
  deactivate Local
end
alt Storage failed
  note over API : Return safe storage error; do not contact AI.
else Grounding available or both sources disabled
API -> AI : await chat(request, evidence)
activate AI
note over AI : Recheck each source's switch;\nreference evidence is not human-approved fieldwork.
AI -> AI : await _generate(contents, structured=False)
activate AI
alt API key missing
  note over AI : Raise AIError 503 without network request.
else Configured
  AI -> Provider : POST generateContent
  activate Provider
  Provider --> AI : HTTP response or transport error
  deactivate Provider
  opt First response is 503, within total deadline
    note over AI : Wait 1-2 seconds; only one retry.
    AI -> Provider : Repeat same request once
    activate Provider
    Provider --> AI : HTTP response or transport error
    deactivate Provider
  end
  note over AI
    Total deadline: configured 1..120 s (default 45).
    Map quota/key/transport/timeouts to safe AIError.
    Validate GenerateResponse; require STOP;
    reject blocked, truncated or empty output.
  end note
end
AI --> AI : Text or AIError
deactivate AI
note over AI : Reply must fit 4,000 characters.
AI --> API : Reply or AIError
deactivate AI
end
API --> Web : ChatResponse(origin, evidence, model) / error
deactivate API
alt Success and request still current
  note over Web : Append both user and assistant messages.\nClear draft; optionally read reply if enabled.
else Failure / cancelled or stale response
  note over Web : Do not append a failed pair.\nKeep draft; error or silent cancellation as appropriate.
end
Web --> User : Reply / recoverable state
deactivate Web
deactivate User
legend bottom
  The collection and dictionary switches are independent.
  Disabled sources supply no retrieved examples; typed text/history is still sent.
  The model never receives contributor/location/notes through retrieval.
  Clear removes browser-tab history, not possible provider-retained records.
endlegend
@enduml
